(Classifying anaemia by MCV) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (CLASSIFYING ANAEMIA BY MCV \(sample notes\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Mean corpuscular volume \(MCV\) groups anaemias:) Tj
T* (- Microcytic \(MCV below about 80 fL\): iron deficiency, thalassaemia trait, anaemia of) Tj
T* (chronic disease \(often normocytic early\), sideroblastic anaemia.) Tj
T* (- Normocytic \(MCV about 80 to 100 fL\): acute blood loss, anaemia of chronic disease,) Tj
T* (haemolysis, early iron or B12 deficiency, bone marrow failure.) Tj
T* (- Macrocytic \(MCV above about 100 fL\): vitamin B12 or folate deficiency, alcohol, liver) Tj
T* (disease, myelodysplastic syndromes, certain drugs.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Practical approach) Tj
T* (1. Confirm anaemia \(haemoglobin below reference range for age and sex\).) Tj
T* (2. Classify by MCV.) Tj
T* (3. Check reticulocyte count to assess marrow response.) Tj
T* (4. Investigate the likely cause \(iron studies, B12/folate, haemolysis markers\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Study tip: "Little \(micro\) iron, big \(macro\) B12 or folate.") Tj
ET
